Patch summary:
Clear a task's border and box shadows when its window decoration stops having
them. With enable_freeform_box_shadows, DesktopModeWindowDecoration sets both on
the task surface for a desktop window and asks for none once the task leaves the
desktop (fullscreen, split), but WindowDecoration only ever set non-empty ones,
so the task surface kept the desktop window's. SurfaceFlinger then drew that
shadow and border around the fullscreen task's unclipped bounds every frame. On
Ika on WSL2 the whole display went black whenever a translucent app such as
Chrome was dragged from the desktop to fullscreen. Set an empty border and empty
box shadows instead.

--- a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/windowdecor/WindowDecoration.java
+++ b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/windowdecor/WindowDecoration.java
@@ -564,16 +564,27 @@
             return;
         }
 
-        if (outResult.mBorderSettings != null
-                && outResult.mBorderSettings.strokeWidth > 0) {
-            startT.setBorderSettings(mTaskSurface, outResult.mBorderSettings);
-            finishT.setBorderSettings(mTaskSurface, outResult.mBorderSettings);
+        final boolean hasBorder = outResult.mBorderSettings != null
+                && outResult.mBorderSettings.strokeWidth > 0;
+        final boolean hasBoxShadows = outResult.mBoxShadowSettings != null
+                && outResult.mBoxShadowSettings.boxShadows.length > 0;
+        // A decoration without them (a task that left the desktop) clears the border and box
+        // shadows its desktop window set: the task surface keeps them otherwise, and
+        // SurfaceFlinger draws them around the task's unclipped bounds under any translucent
+        // fullscreen app.
+        final boolean clearOutline = DesktopExperienceFlags.ENABLE_FREEFORM_BOX_SHADOWS.isTrue();
+        if (hasBorder || clearOutline) {
+            final BorderSettings border =
+                    hasBorder ? outResult.mBorderSettings : new BorderSettings();
+            startT.setBorderSettings(mTaskSurface, border);
+            finishT.setBorderSettings(mTaskSurface, border);
         }
 
-        if (outResult.mBoxShadowSettings != null
-                && outResult.mBoxShadowSettings.boxShadows.length > 0) {
-            startT.setBoxShadowSettings(mTaskSurface, outResult.mBoxShadowSettings);
-            finishT.setBoxShadowSettings(mTaskSurface, outResult.mBoxShadowSettings);
+        if (hasBoxShadows || clearOutline) {
+            final BoxShadowSettings boxShadows =
+                    hasBoxShadows ? outResult.mBoxShadowSettings : new BoxShadowSettings();
+            startT.setBoxShadowSettings(mTaskSurface, boxShadows);
+            finishT.setBoxShadowSettings(mTaskSurface, boxShadows);
         }
 
         if (DesktopExperienceFlags.ENABLE_DYNAMIC_RADIUS_COMPUTATION_BUGFIX.isTrue()) {
